messages:
emily: Quick sync — hitting multiple layout issues on phones when using Console. Tables overflow horizontally, sidebar pushes content off-screen, and the detail button wraps weirdly. Anyone else seeing this? :eyes:

devin: Yep repro on iPhone SE and Android small screens. Table gets a horizontal scrollbar but the header stays fixed width so columns misalign. Sidebar also overlaps the page content instead of sliding under. :iphone:

hao: Good catch. Uploaded a quick concept (see file). Proposed pattern: at <=480px switch table rows to stacked key:value blocks, collapse the left nav into a bottom sheet, and convert some text CTAs to icon+label to save horizontal space. Example CSS sketch:

```css
@media (max-width:480px){
  .console-table { display:block; }
  .table-row { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:6px; }
  .sidebar { position: fixed; bottom:0; left:0; right:0; transform: translateY(100%); }
}
```

devin: Stacking rows is doable but we should be careful with very large tables — virtualize/show a summarised header + "Show rows" to avoid rendering costs. Also need to preserve keyboard nav and focus order when we change DOM structure (ARIA required).

natalie: Found a11y nits: when the sidebar becomes a bottom sheet the focus trap isn't set, tabbing escapes behind the overlay. Icon-only buttons are failing contrast on several themes. Tabbing order inside stacked rows lands on hidden controls first. :warning:

emily: Copy nits for mobile: shorten labels — "Show details" -> "Details", "Expand" -> "Open". Move breadcrumbs into a header overflow menu (three dots) on narrow screens so they don't wrap and push controls.

devin: Quick question — do we want to keep desktop/tablet table layout up to 768px or make a breakpoint earlier? I'd prefer clear thresholds (<=480 stacked, 481-767 compact table, >=768 full table). @hao any preference?

hao: Yes — use 560px as an intermediate small breakpoint for tighter phones, and 768px for tablet. So: <=560 stacked key:value, 561-767 compact table (smaller paddings, condensed columns), >=768 desktop. Also remember 44px minimum touch target for action icons.

accessibility-bot: Automated scan: .icon-action contrast ratio 2.8:1 on default theme (target >=3:1 for large UI controls). Focus order flagged in bottom-sheet pattern. See https://accessibility-report.example/1774100000 for details.

devin: I'll prototype a CSS + small DOM tweak and add aria-hidden/focus-trap for the sheet. Will add an a11y test (axe) and a snapshot for the stacked rows. Planning to open a PR by EOD tomorrow. :+1:

natalie: I'll run regression on iOS Safari and Chrome Android once PR is up and post device screenshots here. Will also test keyboard-only flow and talkback/voiceover. :mag:

emily: Perfect — if you paste the prototype link in this thread I'll pull it into Friday's UX review. Thanks all :rocket:
